  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Fig. 8, 'Example prompts and questions for starting broad and narrowing down'. An inverted pyramid of four bands runs from BROAD (start here) at the top to NARROW (end here) at the tip: TRUST BUMP, BIRD'S EYE VIEW, MAGNIFYING GLASS and MICRO-SCOPE. Beside each band are example interview prompts for health workers: intent and introductions ('Tell me about your background… as a health worker'); 'Tell me about the last time you… registered a new client / provided antenatal care / provided a routine immunization to a child'; 'Can you tell me more… about how you check for malaria?' and 'Can you show me how you… would fill out a paper register now?'; and the 5 Whys ('Why do you… wait until the end of the day to fill out your records?'), continued until a root cause is revealed. It closes with 'Express gratitude for health worker's time'. Adapted from Tran, 2018, under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.",
